WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.135
To show why memorization matters,

00:00:02.215 --> 00:00:05.626
the authors probe the popular numpy-100 problem set.

00:00:05.706 --> 00:00:09.251
Codex-002 scores seventy-two point five percent there,

00:00:09.331 --> 00:00:13.883
but accuracy collapses to forty point six percent
after perturbation,

00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:19.321
and in thirty-six percent of semantic cases the
model still returns the original,

00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:20.731
now-incorrect answer,

00:00:20.811 --> 00:00:25.564
evidence that it is recalling memorized solutions
rather than reasoning.

00:00:25.644 --> 00:00:30.800
On DS-1000 the perturbation drop is much gentler,
about three to nine percent,

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.022
because these problems appear less often online.

00:00:34.102 --> 00:00:39.930
This confirms perturbation as a practical defense
against memorization by future models.
